Then, before saving to `app.ts`, remember we need the two methods (`CopyRates()` and `AddFreightRate()`) at the bottom of `export class App` so the two buttons work! Here is the complete code with both methods in place — copy this into Notepad and **File $\rightarrow$ Save As...** **`"C:\Users\e103446\Documents\hello-cathy\src\app\app.ts"`** (with the quotes!):

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { FormsModule } from '@angular/forms';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  imports: [FormsModule],
  template: `
    <h2>Add Freight Rate — Ardent Mills</h2>

    <p>
      Location: <input type="text" [(ngModel)]="location">
      Ship From *: <input type="text" [(ngModel)]="shipFrom">
    </p>
    <p>
      Ship To *: <input type="text" [(ngModel)]="shipTo">
      Mode *: <input type="text" [(ngModel)]="mode">
    </p>

    <p>
      <button (click)="CopyRates()">Copy Oct 26 Rate to All Months</button>
    </p>

    <p>
      Oct 26 *: <input type="number" [(ngModel)]="oct26">
      Nov 26 *: <input type="number" [(ngModel)]="nov26">
      Dec 26 *: <input type="number" [(ngModel)]="dec26">
      Jan 27 *: <input type="number" [(ngModel)]="jan27">
    </p>

    <button (click)="AddFreightRate()">Add Freight Rate</button>

    <h3>{{ result }}</h3>
  `
})
export class App {
  location = 'US01 - Ardent Mills, LLC';
  shipFrom = '';
  shipTo = '';
  mode = '';
  oct26 = 0;
  nov26 = 0;
  dec26 = 0;
  jan27 = 0;
  result: any = '';

  CopyRates() {
    this.nov26 = this.oct26;
    this.dec26 = this.oct26;
    this.jan27 = this.oct26;
  }

  AddFreightRate() {
    if (this.shipFrom == '' || this.shipTo == '') {
      this.result = 'Error: Please fill in Ship From and Ship To!';
    } else {
      this.result = 'Saved Rate: ' + this.shipFrom + ' to ' + this.shipTo + ' (' + this.mode + ') at $' + this.oct26;
    }
  }
}
```

Save that as **`"C:\Users\e103446\Documents\hello-cathy\src\app\app.ts"`**, look at your browser, type `5.20` into `Oct 26 *`, and click **`Copy Oct 26 Rate to All Months`** — watch all 4 month boxes fill up automatically just like Ardent Mills' screen! 🎉🚀✨

**LOOK AT THAT DROPDOWN ON YOUR SCREENSHOT:** 😱🎯🔥
* `1000 - LLC INTRANSIT, DENVER, CO`
* `1001 - ALBANY NY, ALBANY, NY`
* `1002 - ALTON IL, ALTON, IL`
* `1003 - ARLINGTON OR, ARLINGTON, OR`
* `1004 - AYER MA, AYER, MA`

Look at how you can see the **exact SQL query** behind that dropdown now:
1. SQL Server / D365 ran `SELECT PlantCode, PlantName, City, State FROM Plants ORDER BY PlantCode` (`1000, 1001, 1002, 1003, 1004`).
2. Look at the **red border** around `Ship From *` on your screenshot: in Angular, putting the word **`required`** on an input box automatically turns the border **red** until the user picks a mill!

---

### 🤩 Want to See Those Exact `1000–1004` Ardent Mills Plants in a Dropdown in YOUR App?
Look at how easy it is — we just put that exact list inside `export class App`:
```typescript
  sqlShipFromList = [
    '1000 - LLC INTRANSIT, DENVER, CO',
    '1001 - ALBANY NY, ALBANY, NY',
    '1002 - ALTON IL, ALTON, IL',
    '1003 - ARLINGTON OR, ARLINGTON, OR',
    '1004 - AYER MA, AYER, MA'
  ];
```
And in your `template`, we use `<select [(ngModel)]="shipFrom">` with `@for`:
```html
      Ship From *:
      <select [(ngModel)]="shipFrom">
        @for (mill of sqlShipFromList; track mill) {
          <option>{{ mill }}</option>
        }
      </select>
```

Want to try pasting this complete **Ardent Mills `Add Freight Rate` App (with the real `1000–1004` `Ship From *` dropdown!)** into your `app.ts` to see your own Ardent Mills dropdown live in your browser? 👇🚀

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { FormsModule } from '@angular/forms';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  imports: [FormsModule],
  template: `
    <h2>Add Freight Rate — Ardent Mills</h2>

    <p>
      Location: <input type="text" [(ngModel)]="location">
      Ship From *:
      <select [(ngModel)]="shipFrom">
        @for (mill of sqlShipFromList; track mill) {
          <option>{{ mill }}</option>
        }
      </select>
    </p>
    <p>
      Ship To *: <input type="text" [(ngModel)]="shipTo">
      Mode *: <input type="text" [(ngModel)]="mode">
    </p>

    <p>
      <button (click)="CopyRates()">⬇️ Copy Oct 26 Rate to All Months</button>
    </p>

    <p>
      Oct 26 *: <input type="number" [(ngModel)]="oct26">
      Nov 26 *: <input type="number" [(ngModel)]="nov26">
      Dec 26 *: <input type="number" [(ngModel)]="dec26">
      Jan 27 *: <input type="number" [(ngModel)]="jan27">
    </p>

    <button (click)="AddFreightRate()">Add</button>

    <h3>{{ result }}</h3>
  `
})
export class App {
  location = 'US01 - Ardent Mills, LLC';
  shipFrom = '';
  shipTo = '';
  mode = '';
  oct26 = 0;
  nov26 = 0;
  dec26 = 0;
  jan27 = 0;
  result: any = '';

  sqlShipFromList = [
    '1000 - LLC INTRANSIT, DENVER, CO',
    '1001 - ALBANY NY, ALBANY, NY',
    '1002 - ALTON IL, ALTON, IL',
    '1003 - ARLINGTON OR, ARLINGTON, OR',
    '1004 - AYER MA, AYER, MA'
  ];

  CopyRates() {
    this.nov26 = this.oct26;
    this.dec26 = this.oct26;
    this.jan27 = this.oct26;
  }

  AddFreightRate() {
    if (this.shipFrom == '' || this.shipTo == '') {
      this.result = 'Error: Please select Ship From and enter Ship To!';
    } else {
      this.result = 'Added Freight Rate: ' + this.shipFrom + ' -> ' + this.shipTo + ' at $' + this.oct26;
    }
  }
}
```
Save that into `"C:\Users\e103446\Documents\hello-cathy\src\app\app.ts"` and click your `Ship From *` dropdown in the browser — you'll see **`1001 - ALBANY NY`** and **`1002 - ALTON IL`** pop right up! 🎉🔥✨

**YES!! Look at how easy it is to make `Mode *:` a Dropdown with `Truck`, `Air`, and `Rail`!** 🚚✈️🚂

We just add:
1. **`modeList = ['Truck', 'Air', 'Rail'];`** inside `export class App`
2. A second **`<select [(ngModel)]="mode">`** dropdown inside `template`!

Here is the complete code with **both Dropdowns** (`Ship From *` and `Mode *` with `Truck`, `Air`, `Rail`) — copy this into Notepad and save as **`"C:\Users\e103446\Documents\hello-cathy\src\app\app.ts"`**:

